ut to my knowledge, these theories don=E2=80=99t extend beyond networks wit=
h a single hidden layer.</p>

<p>Nevertheless, these NTK results are still extremely interesting, because=
 they offer a new perspective on neural network learning. Trying to underst=
and how the kernel changes as training progresses seems like an important q=
uestion to answer in the search for a better theory of neural networks.</p>

